    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Disabling/enabling of module core functionalities are expected to be done by user through `vim.b.mini*_disable` variables. [Here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/02e22656f1b78aa9f9a678e0ff31b62bbaf0dee6/doc/mini.txt#L164) is documentation about it. And your case is covered with [this](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/02e22656f1b78aa9f9a678e0ff31b62bbaf0dee6/doc/mini.txt#L199-L202).\r\n\r\nIf you have Neovim>=0.7, try adding this to your config **before** call to `require('mini.cursorword').setup()`:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.cmd([[\r\n  augroup MyMini\r\n    autocmd!\r\n    au ModeChanged *:[vV\\x16]* let b:minicursorword_disable=v:true\r\n    au ModeChanged [vV\\x16]*:* let b:minicursorword_disable=v:false\r\n  augroup END\r\n]])\r\n```\r\n\r\nDoes this solve your problem?",
            "created_at": "2022-09-10T15:04:31Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/127#issuecomment-1242748079",
            "id": 1242748079,
